To generate a table of contents (TOC) for a LaTeX document, you can use the `toc` command from the `tocloft` package. Here's an example:

```latex
\documentclass{article}
\usepackage[utf8]{inputenc}
\usepackage[T1]{fontenc}

% Load the tocloft package
\usepackage{tocloft}

% Define the TOC structure
\renewcommand{\cftsecfont}{\normalfont\bfseries}
\renewcommand{\cftsubsecfont}{\normalfont\bfseries}
\renewcommand{\cftsubsubsectionfont}{\normalfont\bfseries}

% Add the TOC to the document
\makeatletter
\renewcommand*{\@tocline}[2][]{%
  \parindent=0pt
  \setlength\tabcolsep{3pt} % Set tabstop size
  \setlength{\parskip}{4pt plus 1pt minus 1pt} % Add space between lines
  \setlength{\itemsep}{-5pt} % Remove extra space before items
  \setlength{\parskip}{4pt plus 1pt minus 1pt} % Add space between lines
