The time required to become a Certified Public Accountant (CPA) can vary depending on several factors, including the individual's education and work experience, location, and industry. Generally speaking, it takes around 12 months to complete the initial training program for a CPA exam in the United States. However, some individuals may need additional time to prepare for the exam or complete their coursework. It is recommended that individuals invest at least one year of study before taking the exam to ensure they have the necessary knowledge and skills to pass the exam. Additionally, many states require an additional two years of work experience as well as passing a written exam to be eligible to practice as a CPA.
