3. Network Layer (Layer 5): This layer manages the flow of packets across networks. Protocols include ICMP, IGMP, ARP, etc.
4. Session Layer (Layer 4): This layer establishes and maintains connections between different systems. Protocols include SSL/TLS, SSH, etc.

